Package: fmrigds
Type: Package
Title: Lazy, Format-Agnostic Group Analysis for fMRI
Version: 0.1.0.9002
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Authors@R: c(
    person("Brad", "Buchsbaum", email = "brad.buchsbaum@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Group-level analysis of first-level functional magnetic
    resonance imaging (fMRI) statistics organised as sample by subject by
    contrast Group Data Sets (GDS). Analyses are written as lazy plans and
    executed in bounded feature blocks, with fixed- and random-effects
    meta-analysis, ordinary least squares, linear mixed models, permutation
    tests and multiple-comparison correction. Reads tabular, 'NIfTI' and
    'HDF5' inputs (including 'fmristore' layouts), supports space-aware
    masking and mapping between voxel, parcel and label spaces, tracks
    provenance and exports results reproducibly. Integration with
    observation-by-feature 'fmridataset' frames is available when that
    optional package is installed.
